Here's the plan for Acme's billing stack. The change is only supposed to add a tag to the API load balancer. Is it safe to apply?

Terraform will perform the following actions:

  # aws_lb.api will be updated in-place
  ~ resource "aws_lb" "api" {
        id   = "arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:eu-west-1:111111111111:loadbalancer/app/acme-billing-api/0123456789abcdef"
      ~ tags = {
          + "cost-centre" = "billing"
        }
    }

  # aws_db_instance.billing must be replaced
-/+ resource "aws_db_instance" "billing" {
      ~ id                  = "db-EXAMPLE1234567890" -> (known after apply)
      ~ identifier          = "acme-billing" -> "acme-billing-v2" # forces replacement
        skip_final_snapshot = true
        deletion_protection = false
    }

  # aws_security_group_rule.api_https will be created
  + resource "aws_security_group_rule" "api_https" {
      + type        = "ingress"
      + from_port   = 443
      + to_port     = 443
      + cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
    }

Plan: 2 to add, 1 to change, 1 to destroy.
